abstract: >-
  Computational predictors of CD8+ T-cell epitope immunogenicity report ROC-AUC
  of 0.85-0.90 on data derived from the Immune Epitope Database. This repository
  measures how much of that reflects transferable biology and how much reflects
  the structure of the benchmark. Holding out data by peptide, the field's
  standard precaution, is shown to lower AUC by only 0.014 relative to
  random splitting, while grouping by source publication reduces AUC to 0.607;
  sequence similarity is shown not to be the cause; a baseline
  using allele identity alone, with no peptide information, outscores every
  published predictor tested; two published predictors are shown to have been
  trained on 37.5% and 27.1% of the evaluation pairs; and the agreement between
  laboratories assaying the same pair bounds measurable performance at AUC
  0.636. Includes the evaluation protocol, the curated benchmark with both split
  schemes, and the outputs of the audited predictors.
